    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1010">

                <pb facs="0914" n="906" xml:id="pg906"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/16264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-26T14:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>425. Chungking’s 544, October 25, 6 p.m. It is suggested that, in your
                    discretion, as in the cases of recent instances of the endangering by Japanese
                    bombing of American properties, both official and private, you may care to bring
                    to the attention of the Foreign Minister the bombing described in Chungking’s
                    telegram under reference which jeopardized the American Embassy and the U. S. S.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Tutuila</hi> at that place and damaged American
                    property there.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d1010-f1"/></p>
                <p>Sent to Tokyo via Shanghai. Repeated to Chungking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1010-f1" n="45" xml:id="d1010-f1-content">
                <p>This was done in a note handed on October 28 by the Ambassador in Japan to the
                    Japanese Minister for Foreign Affairs; see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_699"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, Vol.
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 699</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
